From 14b76000e75eb803277673a56b237b931e02bc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Parada <livercake@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:56:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] MUSEUM FIX (2026-09-29): stub sthread_get_core_topology for
 the EJS harness

The EJS harness links its own older rthreads (slock/scond/sthread) which
predates sthread_get_core_topology() -- the Sep-2026 libretro-common
topology API that beetle-psx's HD-texture prefetch pool (rhi_tt.c
io_thread_count()) calls at startup. Without the symbol the core aborts:

  Aborted(missing function: sthread_get_core_topology)

Returning false selects the historical 4-worker default -- the same path
consoles take -- so behavior is unchanged, only the pool sizing.

Deliberately a stub, not the core's full rthreads.c: compiling the real
implementation would collide with the harness copies of slock/s sthread on
link. See ~/core-builds/RetroArch commit 40e96ef for the sibling osd_message
wrapper applied to the same core.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 museum_sthread_topology_stub.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 museum_sthread_topology_stub.c

diff --git a/museum_sthread_topology_stub.c b/museum_sthread_topology_stub.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..46da9d80
--- /dev/null
+++ b/museum_sthread_topology_stub.c
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+/* MUSEUM FIX (2026-09-29): the EJS harness links its own older rthreads
+ * (slock/scond/sthread) which predates sthread_get_core_topology() — the
+ * Sep-2026 libretro-common topology API beetle-psx's HD-texture prefetch
+ * pool (rhi_tt.c io_thread_count()) calls at startup. Without this symbol
+ * the core aborts with "missing function: sthread_get_core_topology".
+ * Returning false selects the historical 4-worker default — the same path
+ * consoles take — so behavior is unchanged, only the pool sizing. */
+#include <stdbool.h>
+bool sthread_get_core_topology(unsigned *fast, unsigned *slow)
+{
+   (void)fast;
+   (void)slow;
+   return false;
+}
